contentText:
Quavo and Offset have officially buried the hatchet. Quavo sat down with Complex&#8217;s Idea Generation and talked about how Takeoff&#8217;s untimely death helped mend his fractured relationship with their childhood friend and fellow Migos groupmate.

&#8220;I feel like it eased it a little bit,&#8221; he reflected after being asked how Takeoff&#8217;s death changed his relationship with Offset. &#8220;I felt like it it threw out all the things that I was upset about or that we had friction about. I don&#8217;t know on his end; I&#8217;m just talking for me. I feel like it was it was enough just for me to say, &#8216;All right, cool. Whatever.&#8217; You know what I&#8217;m saying? &#8216;Whatever you going through, I go through it with you. And whatever I&#8217;m going through, I hope you understand what I&#8217;m going through.&#8217; You feel me?&#8217;

He added: &#8220;And I think that, long as I understand whatever everybody be going through and that I can&#8217;t control or can&#8217;t be upset or emotional about that&#8217;s where I think that chrome outer layer come from. That part of me losing my brother and understanding that it can&#8217;t get no tougher than that. So, whatever that&#8217;s in front of me that I got to deal with to make my life more easier&#8230; and to give these fans what they want, I&#8217;m going to do it.&#8221;

He was also asked about the Migos album he and Offset have in the works and what would make them feel like they did right by their late brother Takeoff.

&#8220;Just to release it,&#8221; he said. &#8220;I want the fans to determine that, &#8217;cause I&#8217;m going to put my all in everything and we going to always give it a thousand percent. You know, we&#8217;ve been in the studio cooking. We make sure we keeping everything just like it&#8217;s supposed to sound.&#8221;

Quavo&#8217;s solo album, QRÖMELIFE , will be fully produced by Pharrell and will feature a long-awaited reunion with Offset.

